From 071e92b60d220039999086899e887e2de96b498b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pedro <pedro.portoramalho@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 11:16:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Skip Prometheus samples with counter_volume=None

The Prometheus exporter (prom_exporter.py) collect_metrics calls
gauge.set(sample['counter_volume']) without checking for null values,
which at a certain point (inside prometheus_client/metrics.py) calls
float(value) which raises TypeError: float() argument must be a string
or a real number, not 'NoneType'. When a pollster gathers a sample whose
counter_volume is None and triggers this error, the remaining samples in
that poll batch are lost.

This was observed when a Glance image, in 'queued' state with null size,
was returned to ImageSizePollster, and then prometheus_client evaluates
float(None) and raises TypeError. The samples for remaining images were
lost and their meter series were never created.

Add a null/None guard that skips the sample that would
raise an error, logs it, and keeps exporting the rest of the series of
that batch normally.

Add one unit test covering a poll batch that mixes a queued image
(counter_volume None) with a valid active image, asserting the queued
one is skipped while the active one is still exported as expected.

Change-Id: Ie72bae9a29f59adc5170674b08af55c4687fb8a7
Signed-off-by: Pedro <pedro.portoramalho@windriver.com>
